      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Script Part 1: Open And Frame The Problem\n\n## Spoken Script\n\"Twilite is designed for working with an LLM against a real graph, not just a chat box. In this video, I'll show you how to bootstrap a model, send it the Twilite rules, and make your first successful graph mutation.\"\n\n\"What makes Twilite different is that the result persists as graph content. You're not just getting a response. You're authoring something inspectable, editable, and connected.\"\n\n\"The easiest place to start is the bootstrap lesson. This is the guided entry point for teaching the model the mutation format Twilite expects.\"",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "intro-videos-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1784225885743,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
