      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Script Part 2: Do The Bootstrap Live\n\n## Spoken Script\n\"The handshake lives in the browser chrome, not just the toolbar. Click Copy bootstrap handshake and Twilite gives you the exact setup prompt for the model.\"\n\n\"Now paste that handshake into your LLM. Once it acknowledges the protocol, ask for a very small graph mutation. For example: create one markdown node titled Hello Twilite with a short sentence in it.\"\n\n\"What you want back is graph JSON, not prose, not a screenshot, and not a mockup. Twilite expects a real transaction payload with a valid command and real node fields.\"\n\n\"Now bring that mutation back into Twilite and apply it. If the handshake and the payload are correct, the graph updates immediately.\"\n\n\"This is the moment that matters. The model did not just answer a question. It authored a change against a persistent graph.\"",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "intro-videos-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1784225887051,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
