      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Script Part 3: Teach The User How To Collaborate\n\n## Spoken Script\n\"Twilite works best when you collaborate with the model. If a prompt is vague, refine it. Ask for graph-native changes: recolor nodes, adjust edges, add supporting nodes, or revise markdown.\"\n\n\"Once the handshake works, move on to the primitives. Learn declaration, port, portal, and markdown, and you'll be ready to build real graph-native content.\"\n\n\"If your model can complete the handshake and return a valid transaction, you're in business. From there, the next step is learning the core primitives so your graphs stay structured, navigable, and reusable.\"",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "intro-videos-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1784225888262,
