        "markdown": "# 🎬 Twilite Intro Video (Take One)\n\n## Goal\n\nDon't make a movie.\n\nGive someone a two-minute tour.\n\nIf you finish recording and think, \"That was almost too easy,\" you probably did it right.\n\n---\n\n# Opening (0:00)\n\n> Hi, I'm Mike, and this is Twilite.\n>\n> Twilite is a graph-based workspace where people and AI build knowledge together.\n>\n> Let me show you what I mean.\n\n*(Zoom out so the empty graph is visible.)*\n\n---\n\n# Create Something (0:15)\n\nOpen the chat.\n\nType:\n\n> Create a graph about the water cycle.\n\nWait while it appears.\n\nDon't edit anything.\n\nJust let people watch.\n\n---\n\n# Make It Better (0:45)\n\nType:\n\n> Make it colorful.\n\nWait.\n\nType:\n\n> Do something with the edges.\n\nWait.\n\nType:\n\n> Make the main node stand out.\n\nWait.\n\nZoom around the finished graph for a few seconds.\n\nSay:\n\n> Instead of manually editing everything, I can simply ask for changes in plain English.\n\n---\n\n# Share It (1:20)\n\nType:\n\n> Create a declaration and a reader port.\n\nOpen the reader.\n\nSay:\n\n> Every graph can become something shareable.\n\nPause for a second.\n\n---\n\n# Zoom Out (1:40)\n\nZoom out until the entire graph is visible.\n\nMove around smoothly.\n\nDon't rush.\n\n---\n\n# Closing (1:50)\n\n> The interesting part isn't just the graph.\n>\n> Everything in Twilite is built the same way.\n>\n> Documents.\n>\n> Tutorials.\n>\n> AI agents.\n>\n> Knowledge.\n>\n> They're all just graphs.\n>\n> Thanks for watching.\n\nSmile.\n\nStop recording.\n\nUpload.\n\n---\n\n# Recording Rules\n\n✅ One take.\n\n✅ No music.\n\n✅ No transitions.\n\n✅ No jump cuts.\n\n✅ No intro animation.\n\n✅ No special effects.\n\n✅ If you stumble over a word, keep going.\n\nPeople are here to see Twilite, not your video editing skills.\n\n---\n\n# Before Uploading\n\nAsk yourself one question:\n\n> \"Would another developer understand what Twilite is after watching this?\"\n\nIf the answer is yes...\n\nShip it.",
